    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1016/j.jue.2024.103690",
      "sequence": 12,
      "source_sequence": 12,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "JUE Insight: The labor market effects of place-based policies: Evidence from England’s Neighbourhood Renewal Fund",
      "title_cn": "JUE洞察：地方性政策的劳动力市场效应：来自英格兰邻里复兴基金的经验证据",
      "authors": [
        "Robert Calvert Jump",
        "Adam Scavette"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "Neighborhood renewal programs are a type of place-based policy that aim to revive underperforming localities. The literature on place-based policies has found mixed results regarding their effects on local labor market outcomes, but there are relatively few studies of policies that aim to improve local labor supply. In this paper we examine the labor market effects of the Neighbourhood Renewal Fund, which targeted 88 of the most deprived areas in England during the early 2000s as part of the Labour government’s National Strategy for Neighbourhood Renewal. The fund disbursed almost £ 3 billion for spending on community safety, education, healthcare and workless-ness, with supply-side interventions making up the bulk of the program’s spending on worklessness. Using a difference-in-differences approach, we find statistically significant impacts on local employment. Our results suggest that policy interventions to improve local labor supply can be a successful strategy for neighborhood renewal",
      "abstract_cn": "邻里复兴项目是一种旨在振兴表现不佳地区的地方性政策。关于地方性政策的文献对其对当地劳动力市场结果的影响得出了混合结果，但针对旨在改善当地劳动力供给的政策的研究相对较少。在本文中，我们考察了邻里复兴基金的劳动力市场效应，该基金在2000早期针对英格兰88个最贫困地区，作为工党政府国家邻里复兴战略的一部分。该基金拨付了近£3十亿用于社区安全、教育、医疗保健和无工作状态方面的支出，其中供给侧干预构成了该项目在无工作状态方面支出的大部分。使用双重差分方法，我们发现对当地就业有统计上显著的影响。我们的结果表明，改善当地劳动力供给的政策干预可以成为邻里复兴的成功策略",
      "doi": "10.1016/j.jue.2024.103690",
      "source_url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/journal/journal-of-urban-economics/vol/144/suppl/C",
      "publication_date": "November 2024",
